### Phase 3: Production Hardening & Gotchas
- **Policy Permission Enforcement**: A cluster policy does nothing if users have unrestricted `Allow Cluster Creation` permissions in workspace settings. Administrators must revoke global cluster creation rights and grant access ONLY via specific named policies.
- **Job Cluster Policy Bypass**: Ensure that automated jobs (workflows) are also bound to strict job cluster policies, preventing external CI/CD scripts from provisioning 100-node unmanaged clusters.
